  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through Thursday)\nIssued at 252 AM EDT Fri Jun 19 2026\n\nUpper level flow remains mostly zonal through the period, with \noccasional weak subtropical shortwaves moving across the southern \nCONUS. The sfc boundary left behind the remnants of Arthur will \ncontinue to drape across the area, acting as a guide for any \nsystem to latch onto. This results in daily low to moderate shower\nand thunderstorm chances. A few storms through the week may \nbecome strong to severe dependent on diurnal destabilization. No \nwidespread severe is expected at this time.\n\nA slightly stronger shortwave on Monday may bring gustier \nconditions, even outside thunderstorms. Winds of 10 to 15 mph may \ngust out of the southwest to 20 to 25 mph.\n\nTemperatures to remain seasonable with the minimally amplitudinal\nflow. Highs in the mid 80s to low 90s can be expected.",
